# Component tests

Write component tests in three labeled phases: arrange, act, assert. Render is arrange. Each test protects something a caller can observe: a public part renders, a handler fires, a disabled or loading state blocks the handler, native attributes and refs pass through, and a part used outside its root fails clearly.

Prefer accessible queries over selectors. Do not snapshot the component, assert on class names, read private state, or add a test id when a role, label, or text query works. Each test builds its own state. When a thrown error is expected, silence the console in arrange and restore it in assert.
